  "summary": "The identified studies apply federated learning techniques, described as 'decentralised training without pooled records', to the task of identifying fraudulent transactions. Fischer et al. (2023) report the highest performance with an F1 score of 0.88 on the CellLife dataset [V0058]. El-Sayed et al. (2022) achieve an AUROC of 0.81 using the LedgerGuard dataset [V0057]. Gupta et al. (2024) utilize the ToxiBench dataset to report an accuracy of 0.6 [V0059], while Haddad et al. (2025) apply the method to GridWatch, reporting a test MAE of 0.67 [V0060]. Additionally, Adebayo et al. (2026) explore 'multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling' for fraud detection, achieving 0.82 AUROC on ToxiBench [V0067].",
